<title>USA: Woolworth to close 5-and-10's, change name.</title>
<headline>Woolworth to close 5-and-10's, change name.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Woolworth Corp. on Thursday announced plans to close its more than 400 5-and-10-cent stores in the United States, exiting a 117-year-old business in favor of its more successful specialty athletics format.</p>
<p>The company, named for founder Frank W. Woolworth, also said it would change its corporate name to better reflect its global specialty retailing formats. A new name will be announced later this year.</p>
</text>
